# Think for Yourself, verse m. 2: tune, chord and bass (figure 80.4)
# The bass holds D, then the marked slow triplet E D C (2/3 beat each) to B-flat. The essay puts
# the bass's E (a 9-8 appoggiatura) at the moment the tune resolves B to A (6-5), so the tune's B
# is given beats 1-2 and the two A's beats 3-4.
# Pollack's chart runs on to the bass B-flat at the start of m. 3; the tune isn't typed there, and
# the B-flat chord is taken from the verse chart (fig. 80.3).
#? Tune octave (B4 A4) follows fig. 80.1; it may be an octave lower.
#? Second bar: tune and words left as rests because nothing is typed (the vocal continues on the record).
key G

